        "original_id": "8eeca144-2f3f-5891-943a-c81511fb0e6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Groups: ABBA\n- Songs: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\", \"Elaine\"\n- Albums: \"Arrival\"\n- Musicals: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946.\n- Benny Andersson is a Swedish musician and composer.\n- Benny Andersson was a member of ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- ABBA recorded the song \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus wrote the song \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- ABBA recorded the song \"Elaine\".\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" was released as a single the following year with \"Money, Money, Money\" as the B-side to promote the album \"Arrival\".\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
